#: ../../src/timer.rst:44
msgid "Initialize the handle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:48
msgid "Start the timer. `timeout` and `repeat` are in milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:50
msgid ""
"If `timeout` is zero, the callback fires on the next event loop "
"iteration. If `repeat` is non-zero, the callback fires first after "
"`timeout` milliseconds and then repeatedly after `repeat` milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:55
msgid ""
"Does not update the event loop's concept of \"now\". See "
":c:func:`uv_update_time` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:57
msgid "If the timer is already active, it is simply updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:61
msgid "Stop the timer, the callback will not be called anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:65
msgid ""
"Stop the timer, and if it is repeating restart it using the repeat value "
"as the timeout. If the timer has never been started before it returns "
"UV_EINVAL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:71
msgid ""
"Set the repeat interval value in milliseconds. The timer will be "
"scheduled to run on the given interval, regardless of the callback "
"execution duration, and will follow normal timer semantics in the case of"
" a time-slice overrun."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:77
msgid ""
"If the repeat value is set from a timer callback it does not immediately "
"take effect. If the timer was non-repeating before, it will have been "
"stopped. If it was repeating, then the old repeat value will have been "
"used to schedule the next timeout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:83
msgid "Get the timer repeat value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:87
msgid ""
"Get the timer due value or 0 if it has expired. The time is relative to "
":c:func:`uv_now`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/timer.rst:92
msgid "The :c:type:`uv_handle_t` API functions also apply."
msgstr ""

